<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  JawaGroundHulk.xml                     Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-13
  ============================================================================

  V1 ROW 4, RIDER: the GROUND HULK. The GenStepDef half, 2 of 3.

  Defs/PrefabDefs/JawaGroundHulk.xml holds the stamp itself — the deck, the
  breach and the caskets. A PrefabDef on its own is inert: nothing places it.
  This file is the genStep that does, and Patches/JawaGroundHulk_Register.xml
  is what puts this genStep on the player map. Three files, same shape as
  row 4's scrapfields, which is already deployed and proven (73ca76c).

  ===========================================================================
  EVERY FIELD BELOW IS COPIED FROM A SHIPPED GenStep_ScatterGroupPrefabs
  ===========================================================================
  C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\RimWorld\Data\Odyssey\Defs\MapGeneration\CommonMapGenerator.xml:82-91
  GenStepDef "ScarlandsJunkPrefabs", order 950, is the donor for the class
  and for allowInWaterBiome, isJunk, minSpacing, spotMustBeStandable,
  allowRoofed and the whole <groups> block shape — weight, indoorRuin,
  filthDef, filthExpandBy, filthChance, max.

  The <groups> keys are PrefabDef defNames, read from the node, not assumed:
  ScarlandsJunkPrefabs keys on <Exterior_AncientContainerForklift> and that
  is the defName of a PrefabDef in the same DLC
  (Odyssey\Defs\PrefabDefs\AncientExteriorPrefabs.xml:6-7). So <Jawa_GroundHulk>
  here names our PrefabDef.

  <count>1</count> in place of countPer10kCellsRange: donor is
  C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\RimWorld\Data\Ideology\Defs\MapGeneration\CommonMapGenerator.xml:22-36,
  GenStepDef "MechanoidRemains", which is the shipped precedent for a
  scatterer that places exactly one landmark on a map. There is one wreck.

  ScatterValidator_AvoidUsedRects is from the same Ideology block, line 34,
  and it is the field that matters most here — see below.

  ===========================================================================
  ORDER 940, AND WHY IT IS NOT 960
  ===========================================================================
  Four ordering constraints, all read off shipped defs:

    600  GenStep_ReserveGravshipArea   Odyssey\Defs\MapGeneration\BasePlayerMapGenerator.xml:5-7
    850  FindPlayerStartSpot           Core\Defs\MapGeneration\CommonMapGenerator.xml:167-169
    950  ScarlandsJunkPrefabs          Odyssey\Defs\MapGeneration\CommonMapGenerator.xml:82-84
    960  Jawa_ScatterScrapfields       Jawa_Patches\Defs\MapGeneration\JawaScrapfields.xml

  940 puts the hulk after the gravship area is reserved and after the player
  start spot exists, and BEFORE the two scatterers. That direction is
  deliberate: the hulk claims its rect first, so the junk prefabs and the
  slag scatter arrange themselves AROUND the wreck instead of the wreck
  landing on top of them. Slag landing on the hulk deck afterwards is fine
  and wanted — junk on a wreck deck is the correct picture.

  🔴 ScatterValidator_AvoidUsedRects IS THE ONE THAT PROTECTS THE CAMPAIGN.
  The gravship lands on this map. GenStep_ReserveGravshipArea at order 600
  registers that landing area as a used rect; this validator is what stops a
  73 x 16 wreck being stamped through it. Do not remove it to make placement
  easier — a hulk under the gravship is the failure this line prevents.

  Deliberately NOT used: ScattererValidator_Buildable. It was tried and
  reasoned away rather than forgotten. To cover a 73-wide prefab its radius
  would have to be ~38, i.e. it would demand a 76-cell circle of Heavy
  affordance terrain, and on a rocky or coastal desert tile that fails and
  the scatterer then silently places NOTHING — the wreck just would not be
  on the map, with no error to find it by. The shipped ScarlandsJunkPrefabs
  places prefabs up to 27x13 with no validators at all, so the prefab
  spawner does its own fit check; that is the behaviour relied on here.

  ===========================================================================
  ⚠ THE ONE PLACE THIS FALLS SHORT OF THE BRIEF, STATED PLAINLY
  ===========================================================================
  The brief says the breach faces the colony. It cannot, from XML. A
  GenStep_Scatterer picks its spot at random and takes no argument about the
  player start spot, so no XML field can aim the wreck. What IS done instead:
  the PrefabDef pins <rotations>North</rotations>, so the breach is not
  randomised either — it always opens EAST, a known fixed direction rather
  than one of four. Aiming it at the colony needs a custom C# GenStep that
  reads MapGenerator.PlayerStartSpot, which is v2 work and is not started
  here. RimWorld is top-down and the torn edge reads from every side, so the
  image survives; the narrative approach is what is missing.

  ===========================================================================
  SAFETY
  ===========================================================================
  MayRequire lists BOTH mods, matching the PrefabDef exactly. If Odyssey or
  Gravship Crashes is absent this def is dropped at load, and
  Patches/JawaGroundHulk_Register.xml gates on the same condition so nothing
  is left referring to a def that no longer exists.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <GenStepDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey,Arcjc007.GravshipCrashes">
    <defName>Jawa_StampGroundHulk</defName>
    <order>940</order>
    <genStep Class="GenStep_ScatterGroupPrefabs">
      <allowInWaterBiome>false</allowInWaterBiome>
      <isJunk>true</isJunk>
      <minSpacing>85</minSpacing>
      <count>1</count>
      <spotMustBeStandable>true</spotMustBeStandable>
      <allowRoofed>false</allowRoofed>
      <validators>
        <li Class="ScatterValidator_AvoidUsedRects" />
      </validators>
      <groups>
        <Jawa_GroundHulk>
          <weight>1.0</weight>
          <indoorRuin>false</indoorRuin>
          <filthDef>Filth_MachineBits</filthDef>
          <filthExpandBy>1</filthExpandBy>
          <filthChance>0.35</filthChance>
          <max>1</max>
        </Jawa_GroundHulk>
      </groups>
    </genStep>
  </GenStepDef>

</Defs>
